================================================================================
1. HARDWARE DOCUMENTATION
================================================================================

The overwhelming majority of this codebase is an implementation of documented
SNES / Super Famicom hardware behaviour, written from public references and
pinned to public test ROMs. Hardware behaviour is factual: every accurate
emulator converges on it. No code is incorporated from any of the following;
they are documentation.

  - fullsnes ("Nocash SNES Specs"), Martin Korth — the primary register,
    memory-map, cartridge, coprocessor and cheat-device reference.
    Local copy of the sections used: ref-docs/fullsnes/
  - anomie's SNES documents (timing, PPU, SPC700, DMA/HDMA).
  - undisbeliever's 65816 / SNES timing notes.
  - The Western Design Center W65C816S datasheet (opcode set, addressing modes,
    cycle counts; Table 5-4 is the source for the opcode-length sweep).
  - The SNESdev / NESdev wiki and its community timing research.
  - The published ARM architecture definition for the ARMv3 / ARM6 instruction
    set used by the ST018 cartridge coprocessor.
  - The published Game Genie and Pro Action Replay code formats.

