5. VISUAL INFLUENCES (INDEPENDENTLY REIMPLEMENTED -- NO CODE INCORPORATED)
================================================================================

The post-processing stack reproduces a visual *look*, which is not itself
protectable; the shader code that produces it here is this project's own, written
in WGSL as Rust string constants in crates/rustysnes-gfx-shaders/. No upstream
shader source is incorporated, and no upstream shader is bundled.

  - NTSC composite-artefact pass -- an RGB-domain approximation in the style of
    EMMIR / LMP88959's NTSC-CRT (https://github.com/LMP88959/NTSC-CRT). It is
    deliberately NOT the full technique: that encodes to a composite signal and
    decodes back, which needs a palette-index framebuffer, and the SNES PPU emits
    15-bit BGR555 direct colour. What is reproduced is the visible half -- chroma
    smear and dot crawl. The source comment says so, and says why claiming more
    would be dishonest.
  - CRT pass -- scanlines, aperture mask, curvature, beam and glow, written from
    the published description of how those artefacts arise on a shadow-mask CRT.

RustySNES can additionally *load* user-supplied `.slangp` / `.cgp` shader presets
and translate their GLSL to WGSL at runtime. That is file-format interoperability
with content the user already has; no preset is bundled, and reading a format is
not copying an implementation.

